# doc/codex/issues/0072 criterion 5: the -r run writes a valid raw file, or it
# refuses to write one -- not a third thing.  The status alone cannot say which
# of those happened, so the file itself is the assertion.  The driver deletes
# every path named here BEFORE the run, so none of these three lines can be
# satisfied by an artefact an earlier run left behind.
#
# 'present' is also the hard witness that op-empty-raw.invoke's 'flags -r
# op-empty-raw.raw' line reached the command line: with no -r there is no
# rawfile at all, and all three lines below fail.
present op-empty-raw.raw

# The header the run must write.  Nine lines, 193 bytes, and two of them are
# not fit to assert on: 'Date:' is a wall clock and 'Command:' carries the
# build stamp.  These two are neither.
#
# 'No. Variables: 0' is the whole of criterion 5.  An .op plot has no
# reference vector (DCop() passes NULL for refName, dcop.c:50), so a circuit
# with no non-ground node yields no columns at all -- where the same nodeless
# deck under .tran writes 'No. Variables: 1', its time column.  Zero variables
# is the state that used to abort on the routes that build a plot.
#
# The text is a BRE: the driver passes it to grep unchanged, so the '.' is
# escaped.  Unescaped it would also match a line reading 'Nox Variables: 0'.
grep op-empty-raw.raw ^No\. Variables: 0$

# ... and that the file is the operating point's, not some other analysis's.
grep op-empty-raw.raw ^Plotname: Operating Point$
